 ## Standing rules for every task
 
 - **Migration rule (SPEC §9, §10):** a migration is done when it is written, applied to the LOCAL database, its 
integration tests pass, and its rollback SQL is recorded in the migration header and TRACK. Each gets a row in 
`spec-interview/phase-6-meeting-notes/MIGRATIONS-PENDENTES.md`. Nothing is applied online before T15.
-- **Function privilege rule (review P1):** the baseline default privileges grant EXECUTE on every new `public` 
function to `anon` and `authenticated` (`20260610183000_baseline_core_schema.sql:2131-2133`). Every new function 
therefore: has owner `postgres`, `SET search_path = ''` with schema-qualified references, `REVOKE ALL ... FROM PUBLIC, 
anon, authenticated`, and then an explicit `GRANT EXECUTE` only to the role that needs it. User-facing RPCs that 
authorize the caller themselves (resolving `auth.uid()` → `users.supabase_uid`) are granted to `authenticated` only. 
Server-only RPCs (key read, admission/reservation, settlement, usage maintenance) are granted to `service_role` only 
and are called by server code only after the route has authorized the application user; service role never replaces 
that authorization. Integration tests call each server-only RPC directly as `anon` and `authenticated` and expect 
denial.
